    body: "Editor note: open [Hypertensive emergency (adult)](#/tree/hypertensive-emergency-adult/node/hypertensive-emergency-adult-agent-by-organ) for blood pressure, the [Seizure hub](#/tree/seizure-hub) for a first seizure and the [Altered mental status hub](#/tree/altered-mental-status-hub) for the confusion work-up.\n\u2022 Tacrolimus labels (7.2) list nicardipine as a mild or moderate CYP3A inhibitor that \"May increase tacrolimus whole blood trough concentrations and increase the risk of serious adverse reactions (e.g., neurotoxicity, QT prolongation)\"; cyclosporine labels list it among drugs that increase cyclosporine concentrations. [1,2,3,4,5,6]\n\u2022 App content: Hypertensive Emergency (Adult), node hypertensive-emergency-adult-agent-nicardipine (line 169): \"Nicardipine IV infusion is a common titratable choice when no exception applies\".\n\nEditor note: related pages are [toxicity and levels](#/tree/transplant-patient-ed/node/tpe-cni-toxicity), [brain](#/tree/transplant-patient-ed/node/tpe-cni-brain) and [high blood pressure](#/tree/transplant-patient-ed/node/tpe-cni-hypertension).\n\nEditor note: disposition is decided with the treating transplant team.",
